---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Geraldine's",
  servesCuisine: ["Modern Mexican", "Latin American"],
  priceRange: "$$$",
  url: "https://www.hotelvanzandt.com/geraldines/",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "605 Davis St",
    addressLocality: "Austin",
    addressRegion: "TX",
    postalCode: "78701",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Geraldine's at Hotel Van Zandt, Austin — chef Sergio Ledesma's modern Mexican restaurant with live music, weekend jazz brunch, and a $39.99 Dinner Before Dark prix fixe.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Geraldine's Menu Guide (2026) — Menu, Prices & Hours at Hotel Van Zandt | Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="An independent guide to Geraldine's at Hotel Van Zandt, Austin: modern-Mexican menu highlights, the $39.99 Dinner Before Dark prix fixe, hours, and visiting tips. Written in our own words."
  path="/geraldines-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/geraldines-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/geraldines-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of a lively modern restaurant with a stage for live music at evening (illustrative, not the actual restaurant)"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Austin
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Geraldine's — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">By <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Firoz Khan</span> <span class="text-gold-dark">&middot;</span> FK Digital Media</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Geraldine's is the restaurant of Hotel Van Zandt in Austin's Rainey Street
      district — a modern-Mexican kitchen led by executive chef Sergio Ledesma, wrapped
      in one of the city's best live-music dining rooms. Opened with the hotel in 2015
      and named for Geraldine, the Rainey Street guinea fowl, it runs breakfast through
      late dinner with live music Thursday through Sunday nights, a weekend jazz brunch,
      and a 4.6 OpenTable rating. Below is our independent walkthrough, written in our
      own words. Note: the restaurant publishes <strong>no official menu page</strong> —
      we say so honestly, with menu highlights from the hotel's official site and prices
      from the hotel's own editorial and event listings, dated honestly.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">605 Davis St, Austin, TX 78701 (Hotel Van Zandt, Rainey Street)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Executive chef Sergio Ledesma</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Modern Mexican / Latin American</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">OpenTable $31–$50 pp; Dinner Before Dark prix fixe $39.99</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Live music</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Thu–Sun nights 9:00–10:30 PM; weekend jazz brunch 11 AM–1 PM</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Happy hour</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Daily 5:00–6:30 PM (incl. $6 martini flights)</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Hours</h2>
      <p>
        Per the official hotelvanzandt.com (accessed October 2026):
        <strong>breakfast/brunch Mon–Fri 7:00–11:00 AM, Sat–Sun 9:00 AM–2:00 PM;
        dinner Sun–Wed 5:00–11:00 PM, Thu–Sat 5:00–11:59 PM.</strong> The kitchen closes
        at 10:00 PM daily.
      </p>

      <h2>Menu highlights</h2>
      <p>
        The hotel publishes no standalone menu page; highlights below are from the
        official hotel site:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Al Pastor</strong> — Berkshire pork jowl brochette.</li>
        <li><strong>48-hour Short Rib</strong> in mole negro.</li>
        <li><strong>Pato</strong> — 21-day aged duck breast.</li>
        <li><strong>Chilaquiles</strong>; <strong>Mole Enchilada Eggs</strong>; <strong>Steak and Eggs</strong> (Wagyu skirt steak, chimichurri).</li>
        <li><strong>Bucatini with Uni butter</strong>; <strong>Lamb Birria Tetela</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Scallop Tostadas</strong>; <strong>Lamb Barbacoa Pellizcada</strong>; <strong>Street Sliders</strong>; <strong>Birria Wontons</strong>; <strong>Tuna Crudo</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Baklava Napoleon</strong>; <strong>Mexican Tiramisu</strong>; pain au lait milk bread.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Prices we could verify</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Dinner Before Dark: $39.99 per guest</strong> — a 3-course prix fixe (per a hotel editorial article, circa 2026).</li>
        <li><strong>Happy hour daily 5:00–6:30 PM</strong>, including <strong>$6 martini flights</strong> (per the hotel's October 2026 event calendar).</li>
        <li><strong>OpenTable price band: $31–$50 per person</strong> (circa September 2026).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Individual dish prices are not published by the hotel — we won't invent them.
        The only circulating dish-price list is an old third-party menu PDF (circa 2021,
        $4–$18) that is clearly stale and not reliable.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The deal:</strong> the Dinner Before Dark 3-course prix fixe ($39.99) — the best value in the building.</li>
        <li><strong>The signatures:</strong> the 48-hour Short Rib in mole negro or the Pato (21-day aged duck).</li>
        <li><strong>The brunch play:</strong> weekend jazz brunch (Sat–Sun, 11 AM–1 PM music) — chilaquiles or mole enchilada eggs.</li>
        <li><strong>The pre-game:</strong> happy hour 5:00–6:30 PM with a $6 martini flight.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Music matters:</strong> live music Thu–Sun nights 9:00–10:30 PM — book dinner late on those nights for the full experience.</li>
        <li><strong>Kitchen closes 10 PM daily</strong> even though the dining room runs later — order food before the music set ends.</li>
        <li><strong>Rainey Street:</strong> the hotel sits in Austin's bar district — easy to make a night of it.</li>
        <li><strong>Pair it:</strong> our <a href="/1886-cafe-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">1886 Café &amp; Bakery guide</a> covers Austin's other essential hotel dining room, at The Driskill.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.hotelvanzandt.com/geraldines/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official restaurant page — Hotel Van Zandt</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.opentable.com/geraldines" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reservations — OpenTable</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.hotelvanzandt.com/geraldines/calendar/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Events calendar — Hotel Van Zandt</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        Geraldine's publishes <strong>no official menu page and no individual dish
        prices</strong> — we state this plainly rather than presenting old third-party
        figures as fact. The <strong>$39.99 Dinner Before Dark prix fixe</strong> is from
        a hotel editorial (circa 2026); <strong>happy hour</strong> details are from the
        hotel's October 2026 calendar; the <strong>$31–$50</strong> band is OpenTable's
        (circa September 2026). Always verify with the restaurant before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related guides -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">More Texas guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/best-hotel-restaurants-texas/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">The best hotel restaurants in Texas →</a></li>
        <li><a href="/1886-cafe-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">1886 Café &amp; Bakery at The Driskill</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— Austin</span></li>
        <li><a href="/supper-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Supper at Hotel Emma</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— San Antonio</span></li>
        <li><a href="/fearings-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Fearing's at The Ritz-Carlton</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— Dallas</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
